{
  "area": "cli",
  "description": "AGSC-09-18: what the transport refuses. (1) A request with an `Origin` whose host is not `127.0.0.1`, `localhost` or `[::1]` is HTTP 403 and runs no tool (DNS rebinding, MCP transport page, Security & Endpoint); (2) so is a request whose `Host` names another host, since a name re-pointed at the loopback address arrives with its own name; (3) GET and (4) DELETE on the endpoint are HTTP 405 and (5) another path HTTP 404; (6) `mcp --http 0 --bind 0.0.0.0` starts nothing and exits 2 with AGSC-E003, as does (7) `mcp --bind 127.0.0.1` without `--http`; (8) a `propose` call over HTTP returns the Proposal payload (HTTP 200, `isError` false) and writes nothing: `dist/proposal/` does not exist afterwards and no file of the Bundle changed (`nothing_written`). The server is read-only.",
  "expected": {
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "foreign-origin",
        "status": 403
      },
      {
        "name": "rebound-host-name",
        "status": 403
      },
      {
        "name": "get-on-the-endpoint",
        "status": 405
      },
      {
        "name": "delete-on-the-endpoint",
        "status": 405
      },
      {
        "name": "another-path",
        "status": 404
      },
      {
        "error": "AGSC-E003",
        "exit": 2,
        "name": "bind-that-is-not-loopback"
      },
      {
        "error": "AGSC-E003",
        "exit": 2,
        "name": "bind-without-http"
      },
      {
        "name": "propose-over-http",
        "nothing_written": true,
        "status": 200
      }
    ]
  },
